                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "level": 2,
                  "text": "AMS 2631"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Titanium Alloy: Titanium and Titanium Alloys"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Product Forms: Ultrasonic Inspection Titanium and Titanium Alloy Bar, Billet and Plate"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Scope: This specification covers the procedure for ultrasonic inspection of wrought titanium and titanium alloy products 0.25 inch (6.4 mm) and over in cross-section (thickness) or diameter."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Product availability:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "[Titanium Alloy 6Al-4V Grade 5 Round Bar](https://qqa.titanium.com/product/mill-product-titanium-round-bar)"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "[Titanium Alloy 6Al-4V Grade 5 Plate](https://qqa.titanium.com/product/mill-product-titanium-plate)"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "[Titanium Alloy 6Al-4V ELI Grade 23 Round Bar](https://qqa.titanium.com/product/mill-product-titanium-round-bar)"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "[Titanium Alloy 6Al-4V ELI Grade 23 Rectangle Bar](https://qqa.titanium.com/product/mill-product-titanium-rectangular-bar)"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "[Titanium Alloy 6Al-2Sn-4Zr-6Mo Round Bar](https://qqa.titanium.com/product/mill-product-titanium-round-bar)"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "What is Ultrasonic Testing?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Ultrasonic testing (UT) is a form of non-destructive testing (NDT), commonly utilized to detect flaws that might exist in the associated material that are not visible to the naked eye. This form of NDT is accomplished using systems that generate high frequency sound waves, between .5 – 15 Mhz. The machine incorporates a receiver, a group of transducers, and a display device."
                },
                {
